IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qla-dates`
IMPORT `qla-rules`

-- Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) -- the questions of the CLAIMANT.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom a right of action accrues and who brings, or proposes to bring, the action -- the injured
-- person, the family member or personal representative suing for a death or for the estate, the survivor of child
-- abuse, the person with a dust-related condition, the person defamed, a party to a contract or deed, a creditor, a
-- beneficiary of a trust or an estate, a person who paid a tax under an invalid law: "By when must I start my action?",
-- "Can I still start it on this day?", "Am I under a disability?", "Is there no time limit for my claim?", "Can the court
-- give me more time?", "Did their acknowledgement or payment give me more time?". Two questions (ss 40, 42) are asked by
-- the same individual when answering a claim: claiming contribution from another wrongdoer, or counterclaiming. The
-- court, the person sued, an insurer and the Crown get no seat: the court's judgments and orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of qla-rules.l4. The time
-- bar is a DEONTIC rule run inside the three "Can I still start ... on this day" questions; no question takes a DEONTIC
-- or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) The State of Queensland,
-- CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld): the claimant's questions`

§§ `Where I stand`

@export Am I "under a disability" under the Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) s 5(2), (3)? You are while you are under 18 (an infant) or of unsound mind, and you are conclusively taken to be of unsound mind while you are an involuntary patient under the Mental Health Act 2016, a forensic disability client under the Forensic Disability Act 2011, or detained in an authorised mental health service or in safe custody under a court or Governor's order. Being under a disability when your claim arose gives you more time (s 29).
GIVEN `am I under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 years of age
      `am I of unsound mind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are of unsound mind (unable, because of your mental condition, to manage your affairs or a claim)
      `am I an involuntary patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an involuntary patient under the Mental Health Act 2016
      `am I a forensic disability client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a forensic disability client under the Forensic Disability Act 2011
      `am I detained under a court or Governor's order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are detained in an authorised mental health service under a court order, or in safe custody under an order given by the Governor under section 647 of the Criminal Code
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I under a disability` MEANS
    `s 5(2), (3) -- I am under a disability` `am I under 18` `am I of unsound mind` `am I an involuntary patient` `am I a forensic disability client` `am I detained under a court or Governor's order`

§§ `Personal injury and death claims`

@export Can I bring my claim for injury from abuse I suffered as a child at any time, however long ago (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) s 11A)? Yes for an action for damages for personal injury resulting from sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of you as a child, or psychological abuse in connection with either, whether the claim is in tort, contract, under statute or otherwise, and also for an estate's surviving action or a Civil Proceedings Act 2011 s 64 claim for a death. Other abuse is not "abuse" under the section. A court can still stop a case that cannot be fairly tried (s 11A(5)).
GIVEN `is it a claim for damages for personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages relating to personal injury (including a disease or an impairment of physical or mental condition) to you, or to a person who has died
      `what was the abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc What the abuse was: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse in connection with sexual or serious physical abuse; or other abuse or harm
      `was I a child then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the person injured) were under 18 when the abuse happened
      `did the injury result from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the personal injury resulted from that abuse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I bring my child abuse claim at any time` MEANS
    `s 11A -- my action may be brought at any time` `is it a claim for damages for personal injury` `what was the abuse` `was I a child then` `did the injury result from it`

@export Is my claim for personal injury from a dust-related condition free of any time limit (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) s 11(2), (3), s 47)? Yes for injury resulting from a dust-related condition (as defined in the Civil Liability Act 2003, schedule 2, for example asbestosis, mesothelioma or silicosis), under any Act or law -- but not for injury resulting from smoking, other tobacco use or tobacco smoke, and not for an older claim (one that arose before the 2010 change in s 47) that has been decided, settled or discontinued, or for which a court refused an extension before that change.
GIVEN `is it a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your personal injury results from a dust-related condition within the Civil Liability Act 2003, schedule 2
      `does it result from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the personal injury results from smoking or other use of tobacco products, or exposure to tobacco smoke
      `did it arise before the 2010 change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your right of action accrued before section 47 (inserted by the Civil Liability and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2010) commenced
      `has judgment been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether judgment has been given in an action on the claim
      `was it settled or discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an action on the claim has been settled or discontinued
      `was an extension refused before the 2010 change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before section 47 commenced, a court refused an application to extend the limitation period for the claim
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my dust disease claim free of any time limit` MEANS
    `s 11(2) -- my dust-related condition claim has no limitation period` `is it a dust-related condition` `does it result from tobacco` `did it arise before the 2010 change` `has judgment been given` `was it settled or discontinued` `was an extension refused before the 2010 change`

@export By when must I start my court action for damages for personal injury, or for injury resulting from a death (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 7, 11, 11A, 29, 31, 32, 38)? Within 3 years from the day the cause of action arose; never, for injury from child abuse or a dust-related condition; if you were under 18 or of unsound mind when it arose, until 3 years after that ended (or you died) if later; not counting until you discover any fraud or mistake; and to 1 year after you learned a decisive fact if the court has extended it. Another Act's time limit (for example for workers compensation) applies instead (s 7).
GIVEN `is it a child abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is one that may be brought at any time under s 11A (see the child abuse question)
      `is it a dust claim with no time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim has no limitation period under s 11(2) (see the dust disease question)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act fixes a limitation period for this action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 7)
      `the day my cause of action arose` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action arose (usually the day of the injury, or for a disease the day damage first occurred)
      `how did the right come to me` IS A `How the right came to me` @desc Whether the right first accrued to you; first accrued to someone not under a disability through whom you claim; or passed to you on the death of a person who was under a disability when it accrued and when they died
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person to whom the right first accrued (yours, unless it passed to you)
      `was I of unsound mind when it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person was of unsound mind on the day the cause of action arose
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unsound mind has since ended, or the person has died
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the unsound mind ended or the person died; if the right passed to you on the death of a person under a disability, the day of that death (any date otherwise)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on the fraud of the person you would sue (or their agent), the claim was concealed by that fraud, or the action is for relief from the consequences of a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any date if not)
      `has the court extended my time for a late fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered under s 31 (or s 32, for an estate's surviving action) that the period be extended because a decisive fact was outside your means of knowledge
      `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` IS A DATE @desc The day the court found the decisive fact came within your (or the deceased's) means of knowledge (any date if no order)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I start my personal injury or death action` MEANS
    `the time limit for the injury claim` (`The injury claim` WITH
        `injury: s 11A applies`                  IS `is it a child abuse claim`
        `injury: s 11(2) applies`                IS `is it a dust claim with no time limit`
        `injury: another Act sets the period`    IS `does another Act set the time limit`
        `injury: accrual day`                    IS `the day my cause of action arose`
        `injury: disability`                     IS (`Disability facts` WITH
            `how the right came`         IS `how did the right come to me`
            `birth day`                  IS `my date of birth`
            `of unsound mind at accrual` IS `was I of unsound mind when it arose`
            `unsound mind has ended`     IS `has that ended`
            `disability end day`         IS `the day it ended`)
        `injury: fraud or mistake`               IS `fraud or mistake`
        `injury: fraud discovered`               IS `has it been discovered`
        `injury: fraud discovery day`            IS `day it was discovered`
        `injury: court extended for a late fact` IS `has the court extended my time for a late fact`
        `injury: late fact day`                  IS `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge`)

@export If I start my court action for damages for personal injury or a death on a given day, is it in time (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 7, 11, 11A, 29, 31, 32, 38)? Yes on or before the last day, or at any time where no limit applies, time has not begun to run or a disability has not ended; no after the last day, unless the court extends it (ss 31, 32). Not answered where another Act sets the time limit.
GIVEN `is it a child abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is one that may be brought at any time under s 11A
      `is it a dust claim with no time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim has no limitation period under s 11(2)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act fixes a limitation period for this action (s 7)
      `the day my cause of action arose` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action arose (usually the day of the injury)
      `how did the right come to me` IS A `How the right came to me` @desc Whether the right first accrued to you; first accrued to someone not under a disability through whom you claim; or passed to you on the death of a person who was under a disability when it accrued and when they died
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person to whom the right first accrued
      `was I of unsound mind when it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person was of unsound mind on the day the cause of action arose
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unsound mind has since ended, or the person has died
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the unsound mind ended or the person died (any date otherwise)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on fraud, the claim was concealed by fraud, or the action is for relief from a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could have (any date if not)
      `has the court extended my time for a late fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered an extension under s 31 or s 32
      `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` IS A DATE @desc The day the decisive fact came within your means of knowledge (any date if no order)
      `day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or would file) the claim starting the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still start my personal injury or death action on this day` MEANS
    `an action commenced on` `day I start` `is in time under` (`By when must I start my personal injury or death action` `is it a child abuse claim` `is it a dust claim with no time limit` `does another Act set the time limit` `the day my cause of action arose` `how did the right come to me` `my date of birth` `was I of unsound mind when it arose` `has that ended` `the day it ended` `fraud or mistake` `has it been discovered` `day it was discovered` `has the court extended my time for a late fact` `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge`)

@export Can the court extend the time for my personal injury or death claim because I learned a decisive fact late (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 30, 31, 32)? The court has the power if a material fact of a decisive character (for example who caused the injury, or how serious it is) was not within your means of knowledge until a day after the start of the last year of your limitation period, and there is evidence to establish your claim. It may then extend the period to 1 year after that day. For an estate's surviving action (s 32), the knowledge of the deceased or the applicant counts, and facts only about damages the estate cannot recover or funeral expenses do not count. You may apply even after the period has expired (ss 31(3), 33).
GIVEN `the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your limitation period as it now stands (see the personal injury time limit question)
      `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` IS A DATE @desc The day the decisive fact first came within your means of knowledge (you knew it, or could have found it out by taking all reasonable steps)
      `was a decisive fact outside my means of knowledge until then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a material fact of a decisive character (one a reasonable person, with appropriate advice, would see as showing a claim worth bringing that you ought to bring) was outside your means of knowledge until that day
      `is there evidence to establish my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is evidence to establish your right of action, apart from the time limit defence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court extend my time for a fact I learned late` MEANS
    `ss 31, 32 -- the court may extend my period` `the last day of my period` `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` `was a decisive fact outside my means of knowledge until then` `is there evidence to establish my claim`

@export Can I now sue on a child abuse claim that was out of time, dismissed or settled before the time limit was removed (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 48, 49)? Yes if it was out of time, or an earlier action was dismissed, discontinued or decided because it was out of time (the court may set aside that judgment and take account of what was paid). If you settled it after the time limit had expired, only once a court sets the settlement aside as just and reasonable. A settlement made within time is not reopened by this section.
GIVEN `does s 11A apply to my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is one that may now be brought at any time under s 11A (see the child abuse question)
      `what happened to my claim` IS A `What happened to my claim before s 11A reached it` @desc What happened to the claim before s 11A (for sexual abuse) or its 2019 amendment (for serious physical or psychological abuse) commenced: nothing; it was out of time or an action on it failed for that reason; you settled it after a limitation period had expired; or you settled it before any limitation period had expired
      `has a court set the settlement aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has, on your application, ordered that the settlement agreement be set aside as just and reasonable
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue on my earlier child abuse claim` MEANS
    `s 48 -- I may bring an action on my earlier child abuse claim` `does s 11A apply to my claim` `what happened to my claim` `has a court set the settlement aside`

§§ `Other claims: contract, debts, deeds, judgments, trusts, estates, tax`

@export Did the acknowledgement or payment by the person I am claiming against restart my time (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 35(3), 36)? For a debt or other fixed money claim, or a claim to a deceased person's estate or a share in it, yes if the person liable acknowledged the claim in writing signed by them (or their agent), or paid something towards it (a payment of interest counts as one towards the debt), to you or your agent: time runs again from that day, even if the period had already expired. An oral or unsigned acknowledgement does not.
GIVEN `is it a debt or other fixed money claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is to recover a debt or other liquidated (fixed) sum of money
      `is it a claim to a deceased person's estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is to the personal estate of a deceased person, or a share or interest in it
      `what did they do` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement` @desc What the person liable did: nothing; signed a written acknowledgement (or their agent did); acknowledged it orally or without signing; or paid principal or interest
      `was it made to me or my agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the acknowledgement or payment was made to you or your agent
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did their acknowledgement or payment restart my time` MEANS
    `ss 35(3), 36 -- the acknowledgement or payment restarts my time` `is it a debt or other fixed money claim` `is it a claim to a deceased person's estate` `what did they do` `was it made to me or my agent`

@export By when must I start my action, for a claim that is not for personal injury or defamation (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 7, 10, 10A, 27, 28, 29, 35, 36, 38, 51)? 6 years from when the cause of action arose for contract, tort, an award, a statutory sum, an account, a deed, or a beneficiary's claim for breach of trust; 12 years for a judgment or a share in a deceased person's estate; no limit for a beneficiary's claim for the trustee's fraud or for trust property the trustee holds; 1 year after payment, never extended, for tax paid under an invalid law. Time runs again from a signed acknowledgement or a payment, starts late for fraud or mistake, and runs until 6 years after a disability ends.
GIVEN `what kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim (choose "another kind of claim" if none fits)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act fixes a limitation period for this action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 7)
      `the day my cause of action arose` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action arose: for an account, the day the matter arose; for a judgment, the day it became enforceable; for an estate share, the day the right to receive it accrued; for interest, the day it fell due; for tax, the day you paid it
      `was the deed made after the 2023 change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a deed: whether it was made after the Property Law Act 2023 amendment of s 10(3) commenced
      `would it have been an overpayment anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For tax: whether the amount would have been an overpayment even if the law had been valid
      `is it a future interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a beneficiary's claim: whether your interest in the trust property is a future interest
      `has it fallen into possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that future interest has fallen into possession
      `the day it fell into possession` IS A DATE @desc The day it fell into possession (any date if not)
      `is it a debt or other fixed money claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for a debt or other liquidated (fixed) sum of money
      `what did they do` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement` @desc What the person liable last did: nothing; signed a written acknowledgement; acknowledged it orally or without signing; or paid principal or interest
      `was it made to me or my agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that acknowledgement or payment was made to you or your agent
      `the day of the acknowledgement or last payment` IS A DATE @desc The day of the acknowledgement or the last payment (any date if none)
      `how did the right come to me` IS A `How the right came to me` @desc Whether the right first accrued to you; first accrued to someone not under a disability through whom you claim; or passed to you on the death of a person who was under a disability when it accrued and when they died
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person to whom the right first accrued
      `was I of unsound mind when it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person was of unsound mind on the day the right accrued
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unsound mind has since ended, or the person has died
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended or the person died; or the day of the death of the person under a disability from whom the right passed to you (any date otherwise)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on the fraud of the person you would sue (or their agent), the claim was concealed by that fraud, or the action is for relief from the consequences of a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have discovered the fraud or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could have (any date if not)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I start my action` MEANS
    `the time limit for the claim` (`The claim` WITH
        `claim kind`                              IS `what kind of claim`
        `another Act sets the period`             IS `does another Act set the time limit`
        `accrual day`                             IS `the day my cause of action arose`
        `deed made after the 2023 amendment`      IS `was the deed made after the 2023 change`
        `an overpayment anyway`                   IS `would it have been an overpayment anyway`
        `a future interest`                       IS `is it a future interest`
        `the interest has fallen into possession` IS `has it fallen into possession`
        `possession day`                          IS `the day it fell into possession`
        `a liquidated claim`                      IS `is it a debt or other fixed money claim`
        `acknowledgement`                         IS `what did they do`
        `acknowledged to me or my agent`          IS `was it made to me or my agent`
        `acknowledgement day`                     IS `the day of the acknowledgement or last payment`
        `claim disability`                        IS (`Disability facts` WITH
            `how the right came`         IS `how did the right come to me`
            `birth day`                  IS `my date of birth`
            `of unsound mind at accrual` IS `was I of unsound mind when it arose`
            `unsound mind has ended`     IS `has that ended`
            `disability end day`         IS `the day it ended`)
        `claim fraud or mistake`                  IS `fraud or mistake`
        `claim fraud discovered`                  IS `has it been discovered`
        `claim fraud discovery day`               IS `day it was discovered`)

@export If I start my action (not for personal injury or defamation) on a given day, is it in time (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 7, 10, 10A, 27, 28, 29, 35, 36, 38, 51)? Yes on or before the last day, or at any time where no limit applies, time has not begun to run or a disability has not ended; no after the last day. Not answered where another Act sets the time limit or the claim is outside this encoding.
GIVEN `what kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc The kind of claim (choose "another kind of claim" if none fits)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act fixes a limitation period for this action (s 7)
      `the day my cause of action arose` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action arose (for a judgment, the day it became enforceable; for tax, the day you paid it)
      `was the deed made after the 2023 change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a deed: whether it was made after the Property Law Act 2023 amendment of s 10(3) commenced
      `would it have been an overpayment anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For tax: whether the amount would have been an overpayment even if the law had been valid
      `is it a future interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a beneficiary's claim: whether your interest is a future interest
      `has it fallen into possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that future interest has fallen into possession
      `the day it fell into possession` IS A DATE @desc The day it fell into possession (any date if not)
      `is it a debt or other fixed money claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for a debt or other liquidated sum
      `what did they do` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement` @desc What the person liable last did: nothing; signed a written acknowledgement; acknowledged it orally or without signing; or paid principal or interest
      `was it made to me or my agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made to you or your agent
      `the day of the acknowledgement or last payment` IS A DATE @desc The day of the acknowledgement or last payment (any date if none)
      `how did the right come to me` IS A `How the right came to me` @desc How the right came to you (see the time limit question)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the person to whom the right first accrued
      `was I of unsound mind when it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person was of unsound mind on the day the right accrued
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unsound mind has since ended, or the person has died
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended or the person died (any date otherwise)
      `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is based on fraud, concealed by fraud, or for relief from a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have discovered it, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could have (any date if not)
      `day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or would file) the claim starting the action, or serve the notice starting an arbitration (s 41(3))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still start my action on this day` MEANS
    `an action commenced on` `day I start` `is in time under` (`By when must I start my action` `what kind of claim` `does another Act set the time limit` `the day my cause of action arose` `was the deed made after the 2023 change` `would it have been an overpayment anyway` `is it a future interest` `has it fallen into possession` `the day it fell into possession` `is it a debt or other fixed money claim` `what did they do` `was it made to me or my agent` `the day of the acknowledgement or last payment` `how did the right come to me` `my date of birth` `was I of unsound mind when it arose` `has that ended` `the day it ended` `fraud or mistake` `has it been discovered` `day it was discovered`)

§§ `Defamation claims`
-- Arises only for a person who has been defamed ("Has this happened to you?").

@export From what day does the time limit for my defamation claim run (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 10AA(4), 10AB)? From the day the matter was published (for matter online or sent electronically, the day it was first uploaded or sent). But if the same publisher, or its employee, contractor or associated entity, later published substantially the same matter that it had first published to the public, time for the later publication runs from the first publication, unless the later one was published in a materially different manner.
GIVEN `the day it was published` IS A DATE @desc The day the matter you complain of was published (for electronic matter, first uploaded or sent)
      `is it a republication by the first publisher or an associate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a later publication, by the person who first published substantially the same matter to the public or by their employee, contractor or associated entity
      `the day of the first publication` IS A DATE @desc The day of that first publication (any date if not a republication)
      `was it published in a materially different manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the later publication's manner (for example its prominence or extent) was materially different from the first publication's
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day does my defamation time run` MEANS
    `s 10AB -- the day my defamation action is taken to accrue` `the day it was published` `is it a republication by the first publisher or an associate` `the day of the first publication` `was it published in a materially different manner`

@export By when must I start my defamation action (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 10AA, 29, 32A, 50)? Within 1 year from publication. If you gave the publisher a concerns notice in the last 56 days of that year, you have until 56 days after the notice. A court may extend it, up to 3 years from publication, if just and reasonable. If you were under 18 or of unsound mind when it was published, until 6 years after that ended, if later. For matter published before the 2021 amendments commenced, not answered.
GIVEN `the day my time runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day the time runs from (see the question on that: usually the day of publication)
      `was it published after the 2021 change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter was published after the Defamation (Model Provisions) and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2021 amendment of s 10AA commenced
      `did I give a concerns notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the publisher a concerns notice under the Defamation Act 2005, s 12A
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the concerns notice (any date if not)
      `has a court extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has extended the limitation period under s 32A
      `the day it was extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period as the court extended it (any date if not)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `was I of unsound mind when it was published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were of unsound mind on the day your time runs from
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that has since ended
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended (any date if not)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I start my defamation action` MEANS
    `the time limit for the defamation claim` (`The defamation claim` WITH
        `defamation: accrual day`              IS `the day my time runs from`
        `defamation: after the 2021 amendment` IS `was it published after the 2021 change`
        `defamation: concerns notice given`    IS `did I give a concerns notice`
        `defamation: notice day`               IS `the day I gave it`
        `defamation: court extended`           IS `has a court extended my time`
        `defamation: extended to`              IS `the day it was extended to`
        `defamation: disability`               IS (`Disability facts` WITH
            `how the right came`         IS `it first accrued to me`
            `birth day`                  IS `my date of birth`
            `of unsound mind at accrual` IS `was I of unsound mind when it was published`
            `unsound mind has ended`     IS `has that ended`
            `disability end day`         IS `the day it ended`))

@export If I start my defamation action on a given day, is it in time (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) ss 10AA, 29, 32A, 50)? Yes on or before the last day (after any concerns notice, court extension or disability); no after it, unless a court extends it under s 32A, which it may do even after the period has ended.
GIVEN `the day my time runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day the time runs from (usually the day of publication)
      `was it published after the 2021 change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter was published after the 2021 amendment of s 10AA commenced
      `did I give a concerns notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the publisher a concerns notice
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave it (any date if not)
      `has a court extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has extended the period under s 32A
      `the day it was extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day as extended (any date if not)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `was I of unsound mind when it was published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were of unsound mind on the day your time runs from
      `has that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that has since ended
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended (any date if not)
      `day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or would file) the claim starting the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still start my defamation action on this day` MEANS
    `an action commenced on` `day I start` `is in time under` (`By when must I start my defamation action` `the day my time runs from` `was it published after the 2021 change` `did I give a concerns notice` `the day I gave it` `has a court extended my time` `the day it was extended to` `my date of birth` `was I of unsound mind when it was published` `has that ended` `the day it ended`)

@export What is the latest day to which a court can extend the time for my defamation action (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) s 32A)? 3 years from the day the time runs from. The court may extend it if you satisfy it that it is just and reasonable, having regard to your delay and its reasons, when you learned the facts, and what evidence has been lost; you may apply even after the 1-year period has ended.
GIVEN `the day my time runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day the time runs from (usually the day of publication)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the latest day a court can extend my defamation time to` MEANS
    `s 32A -- the latest day a court can extend to` `the day my time runs from`

§§ `When I am answering a claim`
-- Arises only for a person who has been sued or has settled a claim against them ("Has this happened to you?").

@export By when must I start an action for contribution from another person liable for the same damage (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) s 40, Law Reform Act 1995 s 6(c))? By the earlier of 2 years from the judgment or award against you (or the agreement fixing what you pay), and 4 years from the end of the limitation period for the claim against you. Where the claim against you had no limitation period, only the 2 years apply. Not answered before your liability is fixed.
GIVEN `how was my liability fixed` IS A `How my liability was fixed` @desc How your liability for the damage was fixed: by a judgment or arbitral award; by an agreement with the person who had the claim fixing the amount; or not yet
      `the day it was fixed` IS A DATE @desc The day the judgment was given, the award made or the agreement made (any date if not yet)
      `did the claim against me have a limitation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action against you had a limitation period under this or another Act (a child abuse or dust disease claim has none)
      `the last day for the claim against me` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the limitation period for the claim against you (any date if none)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I claim contribution` MEANS
    `s 40 -- the time limit for my contribution claim` `how was my liability fixed` `the day it was fixed` `did the claim against me have a limitation period` `the last day for the claim against me`

@export If I make a counterclaim or claim a set-off, on what day is it taken to have been started (Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) s 42)? On the day the action against you was started: it is treated as a separate action begun on that day, so it is in time if it was in time then.
GIVEN `the day the action against me was started` IS A DATE @desc The day the action in which you plead the set-off or counterclaim was started
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day is my counterclaim taken to have started` MEANS
    `s 42 -- the day my counterclaim is taken to be commenced` `the day the action against me was started`
